# Notebooks are JSON with embedded outputs and execution counts. A three-way text merge
# produces syntactically broken JSON far more often than it produces a useful result, so
# treat them as unmergeable: a conflict then means "choose a side" rather than "hand-repair
# a mangled file". Resolve with `git checkout --ours <nb>` or `--theirs <nb>`.
#
# This matters because this fork tracks an upstream that edits the same workshop notebooks.
*.ipynb -merge

# Keep line endings stable across the Windows checkouts and the Linux capsule.
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
code/run text eol=lf
